# Per-host SSH entries for bwssh.
#
# Managed by `bwssh add-host` and mirrored to
# %USERPROFILE%\.ssh\bwSshBridgeHosts.conf on Windows so it survives WSL
# reinstalls and can be copied to other machines. This file is yours.
#
# These entries are OS-neutral: the global `Host *` block (in ~/.ssh/config on
# WSL and in %USERPROFILE%\.ssh\config on Windows) supplies
# `PubkeyAuthentication unbound`, so it is not repeated per host.
#
# IdentityFile names a key, not a host: many hosts may share one key. Set a
# default with `bwssh default-key <vault-item>`; `add-host --key <name>`
# overrides it for one host, and `--new-key` creates a per-host key.
#
# Example entry (created automatically by `bwssh add-host`):
#
# Host myserver
#     HostName 10.0.0.5
#     User alice
#     Port 2222
#     IdentityFile ~/.ssh/sharedkey.pub
#     IdentitiesOnly yes
